Send the AP's own requests on the primary stack only

Five requests went out on both control stacks where stock sends them on one.
Counted over the same 220 s window, identical firmware (Android B-16035863 vs
pmOS r36), AP->CP requests per channel:

    msgid                            A.f5  A.f6  P.f5  P.f6
    0x0404                              1     0     1     1
    0x090b                              1     0     1     1
    0x0949  SET_AP_SYSTEM_TIME          1     0     1     1
    0x1307                              1     0     1     1
    0x4605  OEM_CONFIG                  1     0     1     1

None of the five says anything about a subscription. The AP's clock is the AP's
-- SET_AP_SYSTEM_TIME is stock's very first frame of the boot, ch 0xf5 token 0,
and never appears on 0xf6 -- and there is one CP, so one software version in
0x4605. DEVICE_INFO, by contrast, does go to both (tokens 0x0001 on f6 and
0x0004 on f5), so this is not "stock only configures one stack".

Three of them come from the boot-parity table, which is captured from a single
stack and so cannot tell per-stack traffic from AP-wide traffic. Rather than
hand-pick rows, the generator now reads the other stack's boot window out of
the same capture and marks any id missing from it. It derives exactly
0x0404, 0x090b and 0x1307 -- the three table-borne ids of the five measured
above, independently of the count.

The remaining two are sent from the boot-config step machine, which already had
this shape for SET_MODEM_CONFIG.

--- a/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-sit-boot-parity.h
+++ b/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-sit-boot-parity.h
@@ -2,9 +2,7 @@
